title: Fiscal Year Settings
description: >-
  Set the first month of your fiscal year, so This Year and Last Year on the
  dashboard and in reports follow it.
sidebar:
  order: 17
---
**If your financial year does not start in January, tell Taskip which month it starts in. "This year" and "last year" on the dashboard and in reports then follow your fiscal year instead of the calendar year.**

### **Set Your Fiscal Year**

1. Go to **Settings → Workspace → Country & Region**.
1. Find **Fiscal Year Starts In** and pick the first month, from **January** to **December**.
1. Click **Save Changes**.

**January** is the default, which means the fiscal year is the calendar year. Nothing changes until you pick another month.

### **How It Works**

The fiscal year starts on the **first day** of the month you choose and lasts twelve months.

| Fiscal year starts in | Today | This year | Last year |
|---|---|---|---|
| January | 24 Nov 2026 | 1 Jan 2026 – 31 Dec 2026 | 1 Jan 2025 – 31 Dec 2025 |
| July | 24 Nov 2026 | 1 Jul 2026 – 30 Jun 2027 | 1 Jul 2025 – 30 Jun 2026 |
| July | 10 Mar 2026 | 1 Jul 2025 – 30 Jun 2026 | 1 Jul 2024 – 30 Jun 2025 |

### **What Follows Your Fiscal Year**

- **Dashboard** – when you pick **This Year**: the revenue and invoice figures, the "vs last year" comparison, and the other year-based cards and charts.
- **Sales chart** – a year's bars start at your first fiscal month. With a July start they read Jul, Aug … Jun.
- **Completed tasks chart** – the monthly view covers the fiscal year, in the same order.
- **Reports** – the **This Year** period.
- **Projects → Profit** – the **This year** shortcut starts at your fiscal year start and ends today.

### **What Does Not Change**

- **This Month**, **This Week** and **Today** are not affected.
- Quarters stay calendar quarters.
- A chart where you pick a calendar year yourself, such as the leads chart, keeps its own year picker.
- Your invoices, payments and other records are not changed. Only the date range used to add up the figures is.

{% table %}
---
- **Note:** The setting applies to the whole workspace and to everyone who uses it. Changes apply as soon as you save.
{% /table %}
